module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.stale_claim_survives_its_own_correct_edit

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data stale_claim_survives_its_own_correct_edit: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "stale_claim_survives_its_own_correct_edit" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**stale claim survives its own correct edit** (INVALID STATE: a prose claim that was TRUE when written and became false through a CORRECT edit made elsewhere -- the deletion of a CI job, the removal of a symbol, a rename, a withdrawn change, or the closing of a referenced node -- while nothing in the citing artifact changed at the moment it became false. ",

    "HARM: THE CHANGE CORRECTLY MODIFIED ONE ARTIFACT AND THE EXISTING CHECKS DID NOT VALIDATE THE DEPENDENT ASSERTION AGAINST THE CHANGED PREMISE. That is the accurate statement and it is weaker than the one this row carried first, which said the defect is invisible to every mechanism we have and that no test, lint, type check or review of either diff can detect it. THAT CLAIM IS FALSE AND THIS PR DISPROVES IT: a review that joined the retained assertion to the changed premise at the candidate tree detected it, twice, and detected instances the author's own phrase-keyed searches had missed. The stale assertion sits outside the changed lines, but THE DELETION THAT INVALIDATED ITS PREMISE IS IN THE DIFF, so the join is available to any reader who makes it. What is true is that nothing MECHANICAL makes that join today and no check is obligated to. The impossibility claim also weakened the row: a class asserted to be undetectable never ranks for a detector, which is the same move DESIGN 4b(1) names when an inflated rung stops a class from ranking for a climb. A fluent, well-reasoned wrong claim survives on readability -- one specimen below passed four review rounds. ",

    "**A RECEIPT WHERE THE STALE CLAIM PRESCRIBED A MEASURED DATA-LOSS ACTION, WHICH IS THE SEVERE END OF THIS CLASS AND NOT ITS TYPICAL ONE, gunbc 2026-09-06.** `gunbc.generated_artifact` `concurrent_divergence_repair` carried a rationale stating that a lane may commit THE DRIVER-LEFT OURS BYTES provisionally for the two design ledgers. That was true when written. `gunbc.generated_artifact_merge_driver` then made the correct edit elsewhere: it MEASURED that exact action as row-deleting across four heads on 2026-09-04 -- each committed a 97-row projection against a base of 98 and an authority of 99 -- and rewrote its own step 1 to take the BASE side and to say explicitly that the worktree bytes are ours and must not be staged. Neither artifact changed at the moment the policy rationale became false, and the driver diff contains the premise that falsified it, so the join was available exactly as this row says. WHAT MAKES IT WORSE THAN THE ORDINARY INSTANCE: the surviving sentence does not merely describe a wall that moved, it INSTRUCTS the action the other authority records as the guard-disarming one -- committing the provisional bytes MOVES THE MERGE BASE, after which the refusing driver has nothing left to refuse. A stale claim that prescribes is a live hazard, not a stale description, and this one sat at the POLICY HOME while the corrected instruction sat at the emitter, which is the ordering that makes it likely to be believed. ",

    "**AND A SECOND-ORDER RECEIPT FROM THE SAME REPAIR: THE FIRST FILING OF THIS DEFECT WAS ITSELF WRONG, AND WRONG BY READING PROSE AS POLICY.** It was reported as a section 3 conflict -- `concurrent_divergence_repair` grants a PERMISSION while the emitted recipe states a PROHIBITION, one fact with two authorities of opposite polarity. Reading the module refutes that. `ConcurrentDivergenceRepair` has two arms and each names ONE route; the selector returns one arm; the emitter picks the recipe by membership; and `gunbc.test.claim.generated_artifact_assessment_witness_test` `only_design_ledgers_delegate_concurrent_regeneration_to_heal` asserts that exclusivity IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. No value in the module means either actuator. So the emitted prohibition AGREES with the modeled policy, and the reported conflict does not exist: the `may` lived only in the annotation, which DESIGN section 4c says no Accepted program can read. The reporter promoted a `//` block into executable policy and then diagnosed the real policy for disagreeing with it. This is the harm sentence at the top of `prose_asserts_an_enforcement_no_operation_can_produce` -- the prose is read as the guarantee -- arriving from the READER side rather than the author side, and it is recorded here because the misreading is what the stale sentence bought: prose that outlives its premise does not merely go unread, it gets cited as authority against the thing that superseded it. The repair the misfiling would have produced was also wrong in a checkable way: editing the emitted step to advertise a choice would have RED the enrolled exclusivity witness. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, and the reason this is one class rather than four: the mechanism is identical -- a claim whose PREMISE is elsewhere, with no link from the premise back to the claim -- and only the severity differs. FOUR TIERS, each with a measured specimen. (i) MISDESCRIBES CANDIDATE EVIDENCE: `v1.compiler.compiler_tests_rust` `ct_evaluation_budget_consequence_falsifier_test` justified an opt-in arm by saying the --lib suite runs on every push; it wastes a reader's time. (ii) CONFERS STANDING IT DOES NOT HAVE: the same file's block above `emit_entry_point_absent_main_rs` announced itself as a WALL 'ENROLLED WHERE IT ACTUALLY EXECUTES', riding a required `cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib` step -- and `.github/workflows/witnesses.yml` contains ZERO occurrences of `cargo test`, the job having been deleted by the 2026-09-04 runner-capacity ruling under declared drop `rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path`. That is DESIGN 4b(1) RUNG INFLATION, and it is worse than (i) because an inflated wall means the class never ranks for climbing: everyone believes it is already held. (iii) THE REASONING ITSELF INVERTS WHILE THE WORDS STAY CORRECT-LOOKING: that same block rejected a wet transport because it 'would have been an inert lens asserting a safety property nothing runs', and the home it chose instead became exactly that. Not one word had to change for the argument's conclusion to reverse. (iv) AN OUTSTANDING OBLIGATION LOSES ITS ACCOUNTABLE OWNER, when that owner closes with neither discharge nor valid transfer; THE CLOSED OWNER MAY REMAIN A PERFECTLY VALID HISTORICAL REFERENCE. AN EARLIER REVISION DEFINED THIS TIER AS A CITATION NAMING SOMETHING CLOSABLE, WHICH CONDEMNED EVERY CITATION OF A CLOSED THING; FIXING THE TELL DID NOT REPLACE THAT DEFINITION, WHICH IS THIS ROW'S OWN CLASS. `test.claim.phantom_marker_type_argument_identity_witness` named `node://adhoc-da8c65c0-b3b` as the owner of a next-rung trigger; that node reached DONE without the capability it owed existing, so the trigger was retirable by nobody. The repair repointed it to `node://adhoc-f044ad97-222` -- THE AUTHORING LANE'S OWN WORK ITEM, which would have closed when that lane finished WITH THE OBLIGATION NEITHER DISCHARGED NOR TRANSFERRED. The defect is that ending, not the closing itself. The same defect with a longer fuse, authored by the change that diagnosed the class, ratified through three review rounds, and caught only by a dashboard completion notice. ",

    "AND ONE SPECIMEN IS SHARPER THAN ALL FOUR TIERS: A CURRENT-TREE-ONLY RETROSPECTIVE TRUTH CHECK CANNOT RECOVER AN EARLIER FALSE INTERVAL AFTER THE CLAIM HAS BECOME TRUE AGAIN -- a claim made false by one change and made true again by an unrelated later one. The clause 'rust-unit-tests is not a `needs` of the required aggregate' stood in `gunbc.emitted_closure_compile_seed_growth`. It was TRUE when written, made FALSE by gunbc#10078 promoting that job into the required aggregate, and made TRUE AGAIN by the 2026-09-04 runner-capacity ruling deleting the job altogether. Read it today and it is green. Read it during the #10078 window and it is red. Read it today AGAIN and note WHY it is green: an unrelated deletion handed the truth back, and the sentence never earned it. SO A RETROSPECTIVE SWEEP -- THE ONE-SHOT 'is this sentence true now' AN AUTHOR RUNS OVER THE TREE IN FRONT OF THEM -- RETURNS GREEN TODAY AND CANNOT RECOVER THE PERIOD THE CLAIM WAS FALSE. AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS PARAGRAPH SAID SUCH A CHECK WOULD HAVE LICENSED THE CLAIM THROUGH THAT PERIOD, AND THAT IS WRONG: a point-in-time truth check ENROLLED ON EVERY CHANGE would have evaluated the clause at gunbc#10078 and REFUSED, because the clause was false at that moment. The distinction the wrong sentence erased is between RETROSPECTIVE DETECTION, which can only ever see the tree it is run on, and CONTINUOUS ENFORCEMENT, which sees every transition as it happens. Continuous enrollment is sufficient for THIS specimen, and saying otherwise would steer a future author away from a remedy that works. That is the strongest argument in this row for validating an assertion AGAINST THE CHANGED PREMISE rather than checking it in isolation, and it is an observed specimen rather than a constructed one. WHAT IT DOES AND DOES NOT BOUND, stated carefully because the first version of this row overreached. It bounds the RETROSPECTIVE form: a sweep of the current tree cannot distinguish TRUE AND PRESERVED from TRUE AGAIN BY COINCIDENCE, because both read green, and the difference lives only in the history of the premise. It does NOT bound a per-change check, which sees the falsifying transition at the moment it occurs and needs no history at all. The practical consequence for a repair is that a currently-green sentence is not evidence of a healthy sentence -- coincidental re-validation is indistinguishable from durability at the moment of reading, and the difference only appears in the history of the premise. ",
    "THE TELL THAT DISTINGUISHES (iv) FROM A HEALTHY CITATION IS ONE QUESTION, and it is decidable: AFTER THE LIFECYCLE TRANSITION, DOES EVERY STILL-UNDISCHARGED OBLIGATION RETAIN AN ACCOUNTABLE OWNER OR A VALID TRANSFER? AN EARLIER REVISION ASKED WHETHER THE CITATION WOULD STILL HAVE A REFERENT, AND THAT WAS OVERBROAD: a CLOSED work item is a perfectly valid HISTORICAL reference, and nothing is wrong with citing one for what it did. The failure is not that a referent ended; it is that an OUTSTANDING OBLIGATION lost accountable responsibility with neither discharge nor transfer. Historical reference and active responsibility are different uses of one citation, and only the second is at risk when a lifecycle ends. A WORK ITEM'S CURRENT `in_progress` STATUS DOES NOT ESTABLISH THIS PROPERTY, AND ITS CLOSURE IS SAFE FOR THE OBLIGATION ONLY WHEN THE OBLIGATION IS DISCHARGED OR RESPONSIBILITY VALIDLY TRANSFERRED. AN EARLIER REVISION SAID A WORK ITEM FAILS BY CONSTRUCTION, WHICH NO LONGER FOLLOWS FROM THE QUESTION ABOVE: a work item can discharge before it closes, or transfer to a successor that accepts responsibility, and either is a clean ending. Checking that a candidate node is currently `in_progress` answers the STATUS question and never the RESPONSIBILITY-SURVIVAL question -- which is precisely the check on which the defective repoint was ratified. An earlier revision called the second one the LIFETIME question, which was the withdrawn framing: what must survive is responsibility, not the owner. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable. The population is discovered by sweeping prose for the dead premise and reading every hit in context, which is manual and has no denominator. ",

    "CEILING, STATED PER SUB-CASE BECAUSE THE SUB-CASES DO NOT SHARE ONE. THE FREE-PROSE FORM CARRIES NO RUNG AT ALL AND IS NOT A CEILING OF 2: whether an arbitrary sentence is still true is not a property the source decides, so no mechanism EXISTS to reliably expose and block the invalid state, and DESIGN 4b's rung 2 requires exactly such a mechanism. The absence of an evaluator is what DISQUALIFIES a class from carrying a rung; it is not a low rung. That puts free prose in 4b's ADJACENT COLUMN -- OUTSIDE THE MODELED GUARANTEE -- which the ladder deliberately excludes so that 'we do not model this' cannot masquerade as a weak implementation that should climb. TWO EARLIER REVISIONS OF THIS ROW GOT THIS WRONG IN TWO DIFFERENT WAYS, AND THE ROW CONTRADICTED ITSELF BETWEEN THEM: the header claimed a ceiling of 2 for the free-prose form while the body said it stays at mitigation, which is rung 1 -- two rungs for one sub-case in one row, neither of them derived. THE STRUCTURED SUB-CASES DO CARRY CEILINGS, and they are the whole of this row's ladder claim. THE ABSENCE OF A GENERAL FREE-PROSE EVALUATOR DOES NOT DERIVE A CEILING FOR THE STRUCTURED SUB-CASES, AND AN EARLIER REVISION DERIVED ONE FROM IT: a declaration-existence check establishes EXISTENCE, not that a sentence stayed true, and not that the named declaration OWNS the cited obligation. Those are three different properties and the check decides only the first. A DECLARATION-EXISTENCE CHECK ESTABLISHES EXISTENCE ONLY; IT ESTABLISHES NEITHER THE TRUTH OF A DEPENDENT ASSERTION NOR CONTINUED RESPONSIBILITY, AND ANY GUARANTEE FOR EITHER STRUCTURED RELATION MUST FOLLOW FROM THAT RELATION'S OWN MODEL AND ENFORCEMENT BOUNDARY -- not from the limits of free-prose evaluation. AN EARLIER REVISION INSTEAD ASSERTED THAT THE THIRD PROPERTY, OWNERSHIP, IS UNDECIDABLE, AND THAT WAS NOT ESTABLISHED: ownership is carried in a `String` here, and a current representation is a fact about this model rather than a proof that ownership cannot be modeled. What IS decidable is the two structured sub-cases, and the ceiling is stated per sub-case rather than for the class: a citation naming a DECLARED SYMBOL is already checked by the parse-phase `v1_compiler.declaration_index` route in `v1_compiler.bin.claim_executor`, and a citation naming a LIFECYCLE-BOUNDED REFERENT is decidable the same way if such referents are modeled rather than spelled into a `String`. Free prose asserting a fact about CI shape is reachable by neither, which is why it sits outside the modeled guarantee above rather than at any rung, and the honest disposition for it is a declared boundary obligation -- observed, refused or mitigated at that boundary -- and never a number on the ladder. THE COINCIDENTAL-RE-VALIDATION SPECIMEN DOES NOT LOWER THIS CEILING, AND AN EARLIER REVISION USED IT TO DO SO. It bounds a RETROSPECTIVE sweep only; a check enrolled on every change would have refused at the falsifying transition. What actually distinguishes the sub-cases is the EVALUATION limit already stated above -- whether a free-prose sentence is true is not a property the source decides -- and not the timing of the reading. That limit is why the free-prose form carries NO RUNG rather than a low one, as stated at the top of this ceiling; it is not a derivation of 2 for anything. The two are independent, and conflating them makes continuous enforcement look futile when it is the effective remedy for every sub-case whose assertion can be evaluated at all. The next trigger names a premise-join because a join is DECIDABLE where a general truth test is not, which is a decidability argument and not a timing one. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, naming the CAPABILITY and not an artifact, and its SUBJECT IS RESPONSIBILITY SURVIVAL rather than declaration well-formedness: RESPONSIBILITY FOR AN OUTSTANDING OBLIGATION CANNOT BE RETIRED THROUGH A MODELED CLOSURE TRANSITION UNLESS DISCHARGE EVIDENCE FOR THAT EXACT OBLIGATION IS CONSUMED, OR AN ACCEPTED TRANSFER TO A VALID SUCCESSOR IS ESTABLISHED; OTHERWISE RESPONSIBILITY IS RETAINED AND THE CLOSURE IS REFUSED. This PREDICTS nothing -- it does not ask whether a discharge condition will ever become true, which is impossible -- it CONSTRAINS what an accepted closure operation may do, which is the ordinary fail-closed move. ITS BOUNDARY, stated because the guarantee is only as wide as the transition it constrains: an external action that bypasses the modeled transition does NOT acquire this guarantee merely because a source declaration exists. TWO WEAKER TRIGGERS ARE RECORDED AS REFUSED SO THEY ARE NOT RE-PROPOSED. (1) BANNING work-item and session identities outright is decidable but forbids what this row explicitly PERMITS, and a trigger that refuses a legitimate program is a different requirement wearing this one's name. (2) REQUIRING ONLY THAT A CLOSABLE OWNER DECLARE A CONTINUATION -- a successor or a discharge condition -- at authoring time. That was proposed here and is WITHDRAWN, because A CONDITION'S PRESENCE IS NOT ITS FULFILMENT: attach discharge condition D to obligation O owned by A, never satisfy D, close A, and let no successor ever accept O -- every field the rule demands is present and responsibility is still lost, which is this tier exactly. Naming B is likewise not B ACCEPTING O. So the authoring-time rule removes the MISSING-DECLARATION state and nothing more; 'claim and continuation are one object' is a true derivation about DECLARATION WELL-FORMEDNESS and a false one about RESPONSIBILITY SURVIVAL, and attaching it to the second was rung inflation of the same shape this row was twice corrected for. Declaration well-formedness remains a real and cheaper subject, and a rung for it would be honest -- it is simply NOT THIS TIER'S SUBJECT, and claiming it here would make the trigger narrower than the failure it serves. Until that exists the honest arm is the one taken here: name a STANDING AUTHORITY that owns the capability rather than any node. A grep, a sweep, or a one-off repair of the known instances does NOT fire this trigger; they are mitigation of a population, not prevention of the state. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when prose asserts a fact whose subject lives in ANOTHER file -- a CI job, a symbol, a step, a node, a rung -- ask what would have to change elsewhere for the sentence to become false, and whether anything would edit this file when it did. If the answer is 'nothing', the sentence is a candidate instance whether or not it is currently true. The corollary for authors: after any edit that DELETES or WITHDRAWS something, look for the ANNOUNCEMENT of it, because the announcement is in a diff you are not looking at. A GREP IS A CHEAP FIRST PASS AND NEVER CLOSES THAT SEARCH -- it can find a site and cannot establish that none remains, which the MEASUREMENT HAZARD below records six times over. WHAT CLOSES IT IS READING THE ENTAILMENT NEIGHBOURHOOD OF THE CHANGED PREMISE: the framing sentence and heading ABOVE the replaced text, the dependents BELOW it, and the sibling surfaces that rest on the same premise. Those dependents are unreachable by any pattern derived from the replaced text, because they do not QUOTE the premise, they REST on it -- 'a trigger whose owner has ceased to exist is retired by nothing at all' contained none of this repair's search terms and went false the moment the rule above it changed. AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS COROLLARY SAID SIMPLY 'GREP FOR THE ANNOUNCEMENT', directly above the paragraph recording that grepping is what failed -- this row's own class, inside the row about it. ",

    "MEASUREMENT HAZARD, recorded because it cost six detector failures across two sessions on 2026-09-05: every sweep for this class returned a CONFIDENT CLEAN ANSWER for the rows it could not see. `grep -c` counts lines and misses phrases wrapping across emitted string literals (2 where the truth was 4); a normaliser stripping `///` but not `//` leaves a comment marker mid-phrase; an exact sentence misses a shorter variant; backticks around an identifier defeat a word-boundary match; and enumerating by premise returns files that correctly RECORD the deletion alongside files that assert it. A record QUOTING a false claim inside its own errata is not asserting it, and no regex separates quotation from assertion. Strip both comment forms and backticks, collapse whitespace, always run a control that MUST hit, and read every hit in context. ",

    "**A RULE YOU MUST REMEMBER AT THE MOMENT OF TEMPTATION IS WEAKER THAN A PROCEDURE THAT MAKES THE WRONG MOVE IMPOSSIBLE** (2026-09-06, import-cut lane, and the receipt is that the rule was ALREADY WRITTEN DOWN BY THE SAME AUTHOR WHO THEN BROKE IT). In the morning a census scoped to `src/v1/04_infer.dag` reported a caller count as a whole-tree fact and missed a live consumer in the handwritten seed; the correction was recorded at the time in those exact terms -- a census scoped to the substrate cannot see the seed, and v1 Rust is still a realization of record. In the evening, the same author ran `grep .func_env src/v1/04_infer.dag`, filtered it to parent-shaped receivers, and reported the result as 'no read of a parent func_env ANYWHERE' -- while `cli_run.rs` was building a ScopeOrderIndex from every completed module's `func_env.name` and walking `entry_module.func_env.parents` as closure evidence. Same file, same blind spot, same day, with the note already in hand. ",

    "SO THE NOTE WAS NOT THE FIX. A rule that must be recalled precisely when the cheap move feels sufficient will be recalled after the cheap move, not before it. What removes the class is a PROCEDURE with no remembering step: when a claim depends on what the handwritten host does or does not contain, INSPECT THE HOST -- read the region, not a search result. ",

    "AND SEARCH IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR THAT PROCEDURE, MEASURED THE SAME DAY: GitHub code search returned ZERO results for `collect_parent_envs` in `cli_run.rs`, a call demonstrably present at line 15991 and found by direct reading. CODE-SEARCH ABSENCE IS NOT EVIDENCE OF ABSENCE, and a scoped grep reported at unscoped strength is the same error wearing a local tool. State the scope you searched in the same sentence as the result, or inspect. ",

    "THE INVERSE ERROR, AND IT NEARLY DESTROYED A MEASUREMENT (2026-09-06, import-cut lane). This row trains a reader to treat a cited symbol's disappearance as evidence the citing claim went stale. THAT INFERENCE IS NOT VALID, and acting on it here would have been worse than the defect it was chasing. A worker reported that gunbc.namespace_cut_subject_roster listed func_env_views_for_import and selective_func_env_view while both were absent from the branch, which reads as a textbook instance of this class; a manager, applying the correct principle that an authority a change falsifies must be corrected atomically with the change, instructed that the rows be deleted in the same PR. Both were reasoning soundly from a FALSE PREMISE: that a roster row asserts its symbol EXISTS. ",

    "IT DOES NOT. The roster's own header states it is 'THE NAMESPACE CUT'S DELETION DENOMINATOR: every authority scheduled to disappear' and that 'after the cut, SubjectProbeAbsent is this roster's success state'. The row asserts MEMBERSHIP IN A POPULATION SCHEDULED TO DISAPPEAR, so the deletion does not falsify the row -- it SATISFIES it, and the Present-to-Absent transition is the only evidence the cut ever consumed that subject. Deleting the rows would have shrunk the DENOMINATOR to match the NUMERATOR: the census would then report the surviving subjects as the whole population and the cut would look COMPLETE precisely because the evidence of what remained had been deleted with it -- roster_is_its_own_denominator, arriving through a tidy-up justified by a correctly-stated principle. ",

    "THE DISCRIMINATOR, one sentence, and it is what to lead with: READ WHAT THE AUTHORITY SAYS IT MEASURES. A carrier whose SUCCESS STATE IS ABSENCE inverts this row's inference, and such carriers are exactly the ones a deletion program produces. A row that is right about an absence is not a stale row. ",

    "AND THE SECOND DISCRIMINATOR, for the case where the claim really might be stale: A STALE AUTHORITY AND YOUR OWN PENDING DELETION RENDER IDENTICALLY FROM INSIDE YOUR BRANCH -- in both, the symbol is absent from the tree you are looking at -- while having OPPOSITE OWNERS and OPPOSITE REMEDIES. One is someone else's row to fix; the other is a disposition you owe. Only reading the BASE separates them. Receipt from the same hour: the same two symbols were live declarations with real mirrors on origin/main, so what looked like a pre-existing stale row was the worker's own uncommitted deletion looking back at him. ",

    "SCOPE NOT CLAIMED: the four tiers were measured on one lane's sweep of one premise. No claim is made that the tiers are exhaustive, nor that the population outside `v1.compiler.compiler_tests_rust`, `gunbc.emitted_closure_compile_seed_growth` and `test.claim.phantom_marker_type_argument_identity_witness` has been enumerated.) ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
